  "_about": "Calibration: lines every 50 px with x/y labels, a grey swatch drawn by a shader and the same one as pixels (do the two strips photograph alike?), and a probe row L1..L16 of own image layers: with the grid, labels and two swatches, L1..L4 fill the app's own connection's 8 layers; L5..L12 are on a second connection, L13..L16 on a third. A photo showing L1..L16 means a second socket gets its own 8 layers (what DukeAPenguin saw on his car); L1..L4 only means the cap is per app, not per connection.",
